WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.197
Welcome to Module 10.

00:00:02.197 --> 00:00:09.202
In this module, we are moving from general Python programming into one of the most important tools used

00:00:09.202 --> 00:00:12.837
in day-to-day data analysis: Pandas.

00:00:12.837 --> 00:00:19.742
Pandas helps us work with tabular data, meaning data organized into rows and columns.

00:00:19.742 --> 00:00:25.887
Think about CSV files, Excel worksheets, database query results, survey data, transaction records,

00:00:25.887 --> 00:00:33.202
or patient records. These are all common examples of data that can be represented as a Pandas DataFrame.

00:00:33.202 --> 00:00:36.207
The goal is not to memorize a long list of commands.

00:00:36.207 --> 00:00:41.092
Instead, I want you to learn a repeatable workflow.

00:00:41.092 --> 00:00:48.497
We will load data, inspect it, identify problems, clean those problems, create useful variables,

00:00:48.497 --> 00:00:53.462
summarize the data, combine tables, and then validate the final result.

00:00:53.462 --> 00:00:58.932
As we move through the module, notice that we will keep asking the same question:

00:00:58.932 --> 00:01:04.352
can we trust the data we are about to analyze?

00:01:04.352 --> 00:01:09.462
By the end of this module, you should be able to take a small messy dataset and turn

00:01:09.462 --> 00:01:13.765
it into a clean, understandable, and analysis-ready table.
